-- Smash history: the sets of 2011's and 2012's Melee majors, read by hand from Liquipedia's bracket pages (round
-- 734's way; Matthew, 2026-11-22: "Continue"). Liquipedia keeps the later rounds of these brackets, not every set;
-- scores as it lists them (none where it only marks the winner). Forfeits (FF, DQ, "-") are left out, as
-- start.gg's are. Made with tools/liquipedia/bracket-to-sql.mjs from tools/liquipedia/brackets/2011-2012-melee.txt.
-- Safe to run twice.

-- Two walkovers saved from Get On My Level 2014 (round 736) before forfeits were left out.
delete from public.major_sets where set_id in ('manual/2014-get-on-my-level-2014|manual-melee-1|7', 'manual/2014-get-on-my-level-2014|manual-melee-1|62');

-- manual/2012-melee-fc10r-legacy (melee): 52 sets, from https://liquipedia.net/smash/MELEE-FC/10R_Legacy/Singles_Bracket
on conflict (set_id) do update set round = excluded.round, sort_order = excluded.sort_order, p1_name = excluded.p1_name,
  p1_score = excluded.p1_score, p2_name = excluded.p2_name, p2_score = excluded.p2_score, winner = excluded.winner;

